<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Mohács</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1526">1526</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-hungarian-wars">Ottoman–Hungarian wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Mohács was fought in 1526 in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suleiman-the-magnificent">Suleiman the Magnificent</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary">Kingdom of Hungary</a>. The Hungarian army was annihilated and King Louis II died during the retreat. The victory led to the partition of Hungary and opened the way to the first Ottoman siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> in 1529.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-mohacs.jpg" alt="Battle of Mohács" width="320" height="244" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_moh%C3%A1csi_csata_(Des_T%C3%BCrckischen_Keysers_Solymon_schlacht_-_So_mit_dem_K%C3%BCnig_von_Hungern_gethan,_Bamberg,_1526).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>When Louis drowned in flight from the <b>Battle of Mohács</b> on 29 August 1526, Ferdinand claimed both his crowns.</blockquote><a href="/empire/habsburg-monarchy">Habsburg Monarchy · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>When King Louis II died at the <b>Battle of Mohács</b> in 1526, the Bohemian estates elected Ferdinand I of Habsburg, beginning nearly four centuries of Habsburg rule.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-bohemia">Kingdom of Bohemia · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>After the Black Army was disbanded in the 1490s the southern fortress line decayed, Belgrade fell in 1521, and on 29 August 1526 Suleiman the Magnificent destroyed the Hungarian army at the <b>Battle of Mohács</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-hungary-1301-1526">Kingdom of Hungary (1301-1526) · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>…most ambitious campaigns: the capture of Belgrade in 1521, the destruction of the Hungarian royal army at the <b>Battle of Mohács</b> in 1526, the first siege of Vienna in 1529, and the naval operations of Hayreddin Barbarossa, whose victory at Preveza in 1538 secured Ottoman naval dominance in…</blockquote><a href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>And at <b>Mohács</b> in 1526 the army of Suleiman the Magnificent destroyed the army of the kingdom of Hungary, whose king died in the retreat.</blockquote><a href="/essays/the-military-revolution">The Military Revolution</a></li><li><blockquote>After the Hungarian defeat at <b>Mohács</b> in 1526, the crown could no longer supply its Bosnian outposts, and Jajce surrendered to the Ottomans in 1527.</blockquote><a href="/state/banate-of-jajce">Banate of Jajce</a></li></ul></section>
